  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-25: "Yes let me know when done and continue with next tasks". Issue #2671 (read it in full: gh issue view 2671) and DI-148 in projects/spaarke-ontology-platform-r1/notes/defer-issues.md. `GET /api/communications/by-regarding/{entityType}/{id}` unions messages anchored to the record with threads whose messages are filed to it by their own lookup (task 177, D-217). In `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationThreadReadService.cs` (origin/master 2ac250cae4: `MaxRegardingScan` ~192, the filed read ~438-494, `ReadThreadsOfFiledMessagesAsync`): (1) when the 500-row scan or the thread budget cuts the result, the response carries no flag (only a [BY-REGARDING] log); (2) added threads are taken oldest first, so the newest are dropped; (3) the filed query also returns messages on threads already anchored to the record, which use up the scan. Find the client surface that renders this route (grep the route path in src/client and src/solutions) and record it in the notes.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE full-stack developer: .NET 10 BFF (Communication thread reads, Dataverse paging), shared React components.</role>
  <goal>When the by-regarding result is cut by any bound, the response says so and the Messages list tells the user that not every message is shown; the newest filed threads are kept first; the filed scan excludes threads already anchored to the record; the set of messages a caller can see is otherwise unchanged.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>Add an additive response field (for example `truncated: true` or a reason), defaulting to false, so existing clients are unaffected; document it in the route's contract baseline if one exists. Order added threads newest first before the budget applies. Exclude already-anchored threads in the query (for example a not-in filter on the anchored thread ids, bounded) or by ordering, without adding a per-thread read. Keep the visibility filter (`callerSystemUserId`) on every read exactly as today: the result must never include a message the caller cannot read, and the flag must not reveal how many hidden messages exist (say only that the list is incomplete). Client: one short line under the list using the existing empty/info text pattern of that component, Fluent tokens. uac-r2 reviews this route (DI-148 row): their review before merge.</background>
  </context>
